# Oracle samples, round r13 (2026-11-02).
# Format: BRANCH | ID | WHAT IT PROBES -> OUTPUT THAT CONFIRMS IT | SCRIPT
# SCRIPT is one batch file; "\n" separates its lines (written with CRLF). Run as a .bat file.
N | N1 | nested unescaped FOR /F inside a FOR /F string -> stderr shows how it parses | @echo off\nset R13N=0\nfor /f %%a in ('for /f %%b in ('ver') do echo x') do echo ^& set R13N=1\nset R13N
Q | Q1 | CALL label followed by a quote -> R13Q=1 if the label ends at the quote | @echo off\ncall :sub"x"\necho BACK\nset R13Q\nexit /b\n:sub\nset R13Q=1\nexit /b
V | V1 | CALL glued to an expanded label -> R13V=1 if :sub ran | @echo off\nset fn=:sub\ncall%fn%\necho BACK\nset R13V\nexit /b\n:sub\nset R13V=1\nexit /b
V | V2 | GOTO glued to an expanded label -> END without FELL if GOTO jumps | @echo off\nset t=:end\ngoto%t%\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
P | P1 | continuation then ^^^| -> abc line only if | is a pipe | @echo off\necho abc ^\n^^^| find "b"
D | D1 | two redirections before CALL -> R13D=1 if :sub ran | @echo off\n2>&1 >nul call :sub\necho BACK\nset R13D\nexit /b\n:sub\nset R13D=1\nexit /b
